With `footnote.options {"spanColumns": true}`, footnotes in a multi-column text frame are still set inside the column that holds the reference. The rendered page is identical with the option on and off.

The same happens for an IDML from InDesign 2026 (21.5) whose `FootnoteOption` has `EnableStraddling="true"`. The import reads it (`footnote.options` reports `spanColumns: true`), but the 3-column body frames set their notes one column wide. InDesign sets them across the full frame width.

